# Entity or value object

A public Domain class is an entity or `ValueObject`. No static helper classes.

- Entity: a unique core thing with identity (the aggregate or an independent record).
- Value object: a value unique by its attributes. Every VO overrides `GetEqualityComponents` and yields every attribute.

```csharp
public class FullName : ValueObject
{
    public FullName(string name, string surname, string? patronymic)
    {
        Name = name.Trim();
        Surname = surname.Trim();
        Patronymic = patronymic;
    }

    public string Name { get; private set; }
    public string Surname { get; private set; }
    public string? Patronymic { get; private set; }

    protected override IEnumerable<object> GetEqualityComponents()
    {
        yield return Name;
        yield return Surname;
        yield return Patronymic ?? string.Empty;
    }
}
```
